# Code Organization - Feature-Based Structure

## Principle

Organize code by **features**, not by technical layers. Group related files together in feature folders.

## Structure

```
src/
├── main.rs              # Entry point only - minimal code
├── app.rs               # Root application state & coordination
└── features/            # All features here
    ├── feature_name/    # One folder per feature
    │   ├── mod.rs       # Public interface
    │   ├── state.rs     # Data models for this feature
    │   ├── messages.rs  # Events/actions for this feature
    │   └── view.rs      # UI rendering for this feature
    │
    └── another_feature/
        ├── mod.rs
        ├── state.rs
        ├── messages.rs
        └── view.rs
```

## File Responsibilities

- **`mod.rs`** - Public API of the feature, re-exports what other features need
- **`state.rs`** - Data structures, application state for this feature
- **`messages.rs`** - Events, actions, messages this feature can handle
- **`view.rs`** - UI rendering logic using Iced

## Rules

1. Each feature is self-contained in one folder
2. Features communicate through public interfaces defined in `mod.rs`
3. Keep features independent - minimal cross-feature dependencies
4. If files grow large, split into submodules within the feature folder
5. Delete entire feature by removing its folder

## Benefits

- Clear feature boundaries
- Easy to find related code
- Simple to add/remove features
- No "junk drawer" folders with mixed concerns
